bio: Hi, my name is Luna Ortega. I’m currently based in Europe and slowly building a creative career that allows me to express myself freely. I’ve always been drawn to aesthetics, people, and stories — that’s how I found my way into this world. I would describe myself as calm on the outside, but curious and passionate underneath. I enjoy discovering new places, long walks with music in my headphones, late conversations that go a little deeper than expected, and moments when time seems to slow down. I love good coffee, dark chocolate, and comfort food — especially pasta. My favorite animals are cats, because they remind me a lot of myself: independent, affectionate on their own terms, and a little mysterious. I enjoy the gym and staying active, but I also appreciate quiet nights in with a few close friends, candles, and good music. That said, every now and then I do love a wild night out, getting dressed up and dancing until morning. I can be a flirt — playful, subtle, never forced. I believe attraction is all about energy, not effort. If I could live anywhere in the world, it would be somewhere by the sea — Italy or the south of France — warm air, slow mornings, and beautiful sunsets. My music taste changes with my mood, but I’m drawn to moody electronic, deep beats, and anything with atmosphere. Most days I’m a jeans and T-shirt kind of girl, but give me a reason and I’ll choose a dress and heels without hesitation. I don't believe in love at first sight, but, chemistry, absolutely!
